  "id": "n-prefer-global-url-search-params",
  "revision": 2,
  "mode": "steer",
  "description": "eslint-plugin-n 18.4.1 n/prefer-global/url-search-params (default \"always\"): `URLSearchParams` read from the url module as ReferenceTracker (legacy mode) finds it \u2014 `require('url')`/`require('node:url')` with the global require, `process.getBuiltinModule(\u2026)` with the global process, through constant aliases, member reads, object-pattern properties, import/export specifiers and `export *`. No sourceType is pinned, so each file keeps its own module system (.cjs/.cts CommonJS; .mjs/.mts/.tsx an ES module; .js/.jsx/.ts by the nearest package.json's type, Node's syntax detection where that package.json sets no valid type, and an ES module where there is no package.json). As eslint-plugin-n's own configs (flat/mixed-esm-and-cjs picks per file), a CommonJS file has require, module, exports, __dirname and __filename (flat/recommended-script) and an ES module none of them (flat/recommended-module turns them off). So `require(\u2026)` is reached only in a CommonJS file; in an ES module only imports and `process.getBuiltinModule(\u2026)` are.",
  "scope": {
    "include": [
      "**/*.ts",
      "**/*.mts",
      "**/*.cts",
      "**/*.tsx",
      "**/*.js",
      "**/*.jsx",
      "**/*.mjs",
      "**/*.cjs"
    ],
    "exclude": []
  },
